schwab-gate gate 7: the execd runtime — /opt/execd writes, the install, Windows shells, memory readers, the page port, stopping the unit [st-p8k8]

Stage 3 of the live execution service installs execd as its own user with the
trading credential in memory between Steve's passphrase and the close. Every
agent shell on this box is root, so the six ways round that process boundary
named in the design (§5) are denied from agent shells here: writing under
/opt/execd, running deploy/install.sh --execd (--dry-run stays free), wsl.exe /
powershell / cmd.exe, gdb / strace / ltrace / /proc/<pid>/mem, reaching the
page port 127.0.0.1:8779, and systemctl stop/restart/kill or pkill of the
service. Invocations are blocked; mentions, ls, grep, journalctl and systemctl
status pass. Measured 2026-09-13 against the live hook: all 18 new cases ALLOW
today, all 18 BLOCK with this change, 14 existing BLOCK cases and 30 ALLOW
cases unchanged. Pinned in tests/test_schwab_gate_hook.py.

Prepared by COO; landed by Steve.
